@copilot Remove the global runner lookup from Camel's `SuppressionTest.addNestedHttpClientSpan` in this PR. Add a nullable `String expectedPeerService` parameter and use `equalTo(maybeStablePeerService(), expectedPeerService)` in the helper. Update every caller in `RestCamelTest`, `SingleServiceCamelTest`, and `TwoServicesWithDirectClientCamelTest` to pass its existing `testing.expectedPeerService()`. Remove the unused `AgentTestRunner` import from `SuppressionTest`.

This is the latest direction for Camel and supersedes the earlier request in this PR to use `AgentTestRunner.instance().expectedPeerService()`. The caller should supply the expectation instead of the static helper reaching into the global runner. Preserve semantic-convention key selection, null-as-absence assertions, nested-span suppression, and mapping-aware expectations. Do not create or register another extension.

Keep the change limited to this Camel helper and its callers. Do not change emitted telemetry, mapping defaults, the shared runner, or unrelated cleanup already requested on this PR. Follow repository formatting guidance and use focused Camel coverage for the existing suppression modes to verify equivalent behavior.
